[[2047,96,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Working on the interior rear view mirror mounting, open the cover.</p><p>2. Move the rain sensor slightly.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Once removed, the rain sensor\ncan no longer be reused and must be replaced.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Disconnect the electrical connection and recover the sensor.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018611.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,96,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Have a new rain sensor ready.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Avoid touching the jelly-like\nsurface of the sensor at all costs.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Thoroughly clean the inside of the windscreen\nby the sensor housing. Use a degreasing product.</p><p>Connect the sensor electrical connection.</p><p>Remove the protection from the jelly-like\nsurface of the new sensor, then place it in position.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>During this stage, take care not\nto touch the jelly-like surface with your hands.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The jelly-like surface of the\nsensor should be facing the window glass.</p></aside><p>Close the lid.</p><p>Check the operation of the system using\nthe Examiner or the other diagnostic equipment.</p>"]]